# ModelMux secrets. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored; this file is not. Never put a real key in this file.
# Keys are read from the environment only -- never from config.yaml, never
# logged, and never returned in an error to a caller (SPEC section 10).
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# !! THE ONE TRAP THAT COST THIS PROJECT WEEKS (DECISIONS.md D29) !!
#
# `load_dotenv()` does NOT overwrite a variable that is already set in your
# environment. `.env` fills in what is MISSING; it never wins a conflict.
#
# So if a stale key is set at Windows User scope, or exported in ~/.bashrc, or
# injected by your IDE, editing this file changes NOTHING and you get 401s
# forever. Check with:
#
#   PowerShell   [Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable('GROQ_API_KEY','User')
#   bash/zsh     echo "${GROQ_API_KEY:-unset}"
#
# Clear a persistent one with:
#
#   PowerShell   [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable('GROQ_API_KEY',$null,'User')
#   bash/zsh     remove the export from ~/.bashrc / ~/.zshrc / ~/.profile
#
# Then OPEN A NEW TERMINAL. Removing a persistent variable does not clean
# processes that already read it -- environment is copied to a child at spawn
# time, not shared, so your existing shell keeps the old value.
#
# The app warns on stderr when this happens. If you see
# "GROQ_API_KEY in your environment SHADOWS the value in .env", that is the
# bug, not a bad key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- REQUIRED --------------------------------------------------------------
# Serves the small tier (openai/gpt-oss-20b) and, today, the mid tier and the
# large tier's fallback as well. Without this, nothing runs for real.
#   Get one: https://console.groq.com/keys      (free tier available)
#   Format:  starts `gsk_`, 56 characters
GROQ_API_KEY=


# --- OPTIONAL, AND THE HIGHEST-VALUE THING YOU CAN ADD ---------------------
# Activates the real large tier (claude-opus-5). config.yaml ALREADY lists
# anthropic first for that tier, so this key takes effect the moment it is
# set -- no config change needed.
#
# What it unblocks, all of it currently blocked on this one line:
#   - the tier ladder widens from 2x to ~33x, so the cost saving goes from a
#     measured 3-4% to a projected ~37% and finally clears measurement noise
#   - the quality grade goes from n=8 to n=30, because every pair would then
#     compare two DIFFERENT models instead of one model with itself
#   - the Anthropic adapter gets its first live call (prices are verified,
#     the adapter is not)
#
#   Get one: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys   (paid, prepaid credit)
#   Format:  starts `sk-ant-`
#   Cost:    the 32-prompt eval would be roughly $0.30-0.60 per run at
#            claude-opus-5 rates. Use claude-sonnet-5 in config.yaml to spend
#            about a fifth of that.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=


# --- OPTIONAL --------------------------------------------------------------
# Intended for the mid tier (gemini-2.0-flash). Setting this key alone does
# NOTHING: the mid tier is currently pinned to Groq, and the google entry is
# commented out in config.yaml. To use it, set this key AND uncomment the
# google provider under `tiers.mid` in config.yaml.
#
# Its prices there are marked UNVERIFIED -- check them against the pricing
# page before trusting any cost number that depends on them.
#
#   Get one: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey    (free tier available)
GOOGLE_API_KEY=


# --- OPTIONAL OVERRIDES (not secrets) --------------------------------------
# These are read by the app but belong in your shell, not usually here.
#
# MODELMUX_MOCK_PROVIDERS=1     swap every adapter for the deterministic fake.
#                               Prints a loud banner. Poisons the real Redis
#                               with canned answers -- run `redis-cli FLUSHDB`
#                               before any real evaluation afterwards.
# MODELMUX_CACHE_DISABLED=1     bypass the semantic cache entirely.
# MODELMUX_REDIS_URL=...        override the Redis URL from config.yaml.
# MODELMUX_DB_PATH=...          override the SQLite path (tests use this).
